# Merge requests

## Core

- Only create an MR when the user asks. Return the URL when done.
- Use the host’s real tools for MRs (`gh` for GitHub, or the project’s GitLab tooling).
- Land only after a real review pass. If the target moved, rebase onto it — not merge.
- Hotfix / critical production bug → Hotfix body; title stays `fix(…)`. Everything else → Default.

## Title

Format: `type(scope): short imperative summary` (scope optional).

- `feat` — new user-facing behavior (default for product work)
- `fix` — bug fixes (including hotfixes)
- `test` — tests only
- `chore` — tooling/deps/housekeeping
- `docs` — documentation only
- `refactor` — internal structure, no behavior change
- `perf` — performance
- `ci` / `build` — CI or build system

Examples: `fix(api): resolve location permission race`, `chore(eslint): bump flat config`.

- Pick the dominant type on the branch. Mixed work → primary user-facing intent.

## Body

Fill each section with real content; omit a section only when it would be empty. No commit-message paste. Pass the body via HEREDOC.

### Default

```markdown
### Description
Describe the problem or user story this merge request addresses.

### Changes Made
Provide code snippets or screenshots as needed.

### Related Issues
Provide links to the related issues or feature requests.

### Additional Notes
Include any extra information or considerations for reviewers, such as impacted areas of the codebase.
```

### Hotfix

```markdown
### Issue
Provide a link to the original issue or bug report.

### Problem
Describe the critical issue or bug being addressed.

### Solution
Explain the fix or solution implemented.

### Changes Made
Provide code snippets or screenshots as needed.

### Additional Notes
Include any extra information or considerations for reviewers, such as impacted areas of the codebase.
```

## Create

- Branch name when creating one: `type/kebab-slug` (e.g. `fix/location-permission-race`, `chore/bump-eslint-flat-config`).
- Before create: `status`, full diff vs base, and commit log since divergence — cover **all** commits on the branch, not only the latest.
- Push with `-u` if the branch has no upstream.
- UI MRs: before/after images when the change is visual (skip with a short reason if not feasible).
- Sanitize captures and attachments before upload. If unsafe → state blocker; never upload.

## Land

- After land: checkout default branch, `pull --ff-only`, verify clean `status -sb`.
